Z||000040||fierospeeder||03-27-2001||03:07 PM||||1)didn't come with a v8 or atleast a turbo.<BR>2)84 oil pans is a bit*h to fix, no gear cover bolts.<BR>3)cradle likes to rust, fiero64 said por-15, wish it was true, im going to coat it on my cradle and my vw beetle.  Freaking specks of rust falling in my eye. Just anything that rusts.<BR>4)Not really powersteering, but something to make the car get out of tight areas in traffic when at 0mph.  But i love the go kart steering response.<BR>5)Haze mentioned..... Blind Spot<BR>6)wish pontiac put speakers in chairs in all the cars except the 84, ha ha people i got an 84!!!!!!<BR>7)The crapass paint or clearcoat that fades and is common with a lot of used fieros i see.  Unless its due to lack of waxing?<BR>8)Not a monster truck to run over SUVs<BR>9)Wish parts were more available from GM or dealerships being more supportive, this is for them all.<BR>10)GM to have restoration parts for the fiero, unlike the corvettes, bel airs etc... that catalog they have.<BR>11)Its sitting in my driveway waiting for me to get a new plate sticker.freaking illinois 80 bucks?<BR>12)the stupid stories that they are hard to fix when 100000000000000000 GM cars had 2.5 and 2.8 engines, go to the freaking junkyard.<P>i like the doors without a frame on top, like the knightrider car, you can go fast on turns, suspension is very firm,one of a kind car, not many people have them.||||reg||1
Z||000041||Nashco||03-27-2001||03:08 PM||||I hate trying to get recall work done that was supposed to be done 10 years ago.  I also hate that GM made such crappy plastics for the dashes and trim.  Ok, I don't hate it, but it sure does suck.  I also hate, right now, that my car has been sitting in a storage shed 850 miles away, just itching to get fixed...but I love that I get to see it again this weekend <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Bryce<BR>88 GT<P>Aw...who am I kidding...I can't stay mad at it <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000042||sqoach||03-27-2001||03:20 PM||||not to sound like an ass, but there's no need for a 6 spd tranny, alex4mula. that's just too much shifting for a car that doesn't get above 130 mph or around that. (ok i know that some of your cars are faster, but i'm talking about stock)<P>and however many people think there is no room for a good sub, i disagree with that. unless you think a good sub is a 15" or 18" i could see your point. one of the best install's i've seen was fierosound's. he used two 12s! i think that's plenty of sub.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>and fierospeeder, they made the headrest speakers in 85 also.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><P>i hope i don't get flamed for any of my comments. just stating my opinion.||||reg||1
